Moreover, the availability and popularity of Voidwalkers in various expansions and patches have contributed to their prevalence among Warlocks. Players tend to stick with pets that offer balanced performance across different gameplay scenarios, making Voidwalkers the preferred choice over Succubi for most leveling and questing purposes.

In summary, while Succubi have their own strengths, Voidwalkers provide a more versatile and reliable performance in the context of leveling and questing, which is why they are more commonly seen among Warlocks in classic WoW.

